---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ScreenshotFigure from '../components/ScreenshotFigure.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Live demo — try the planner free"
  description="Try the Ultimate Offline Life Planner free in your browser. The demo is the real planner running with isolated sample data."
  path="/demo"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 1120px;">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal="up">Free demo</p>
      <h1 data-reveal="up">Try the real planner, right now</h1>
      <p class="lead" data-reveal="up">
        No sign-up, no download, no email address. The demo below is the actual
        planner file, running in your browser with isolated sample data so you
        can explore before you buy.
      </p>

      <div class="notice" role="note" data-reveal="up">
        <p style="margin: 0;">
          <strong>How the demo works:</strong> this is the full planner — not a
          video, not a mockup, not a feature-limited teaser. Sample entries are
          pre-loaded so you can click around freely. Anything you change stays
          in the demo only, stored locally in your own browser; it can never
          touch a purchased copy, and nothing leaves your device. You can reset
          the demo data any time from Settings.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="demo-actions" data-reveal="up">
        <a
          class="btn btn-primary"
          href="/downloads/demo.html"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          Open the live demo
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/products/ultimate-life-planner">
          See the full product
        </a>
      </div>

      <div data-reveal="scale">
        <iframe
          class="demo-frame"
          src="/downloads/demo.html"
          title="Live demo of the Ultimate Offline Life Planner"
          loading="lazy"
        ></iframe>
      </div>
      <p class="small muted" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
        If the embedded demo does not load in your browser, use the full-screen
        link above. Like the purchased product, the demo runs offline once loaded
        and keeps its sample data on your device only.
      </p>

      <aside class="card offline-proof" data-reveal="up" aria-labelledby="offline-proof-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Offline proof</p>
        <h2 id="offline-proof-title">Turn off your Wi-Fi — this demo keeps working.</h2>
        <p>
          The demo is one self-contained file: no servers, no tracking, no
          requests after it loads. Load it once, then go offline — everything
          still works. The purchased planner works exactly the same way.
        </p>
        <p class="offline-status" role="status">
          <span class="offline-dot" id="offline-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span id="offline-text">Checking your connection…</span>
        </p>
        <p class="small muted" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
          Try it: turn off Wi-Fi or switch on airplane mode, then click around
          the demo above — add a task, log a habit, change a setting. It all
          still works, because there is nothing to stop working.
        </p>
      </aside>
      <script>
        const initOfflineProof = () => {
          const dot = document.getElementById('offline-dot');
          const text = document.getElementById('offline-text');
          if (!dot || !text) return;
          const update = () => {
            const online = navigator.onLine;
            dot.classList.toggle('is-offline', !online);
            text.textContent = online
              ? 'You\u2019re online right now — go offline and keep clicking. Nothing breaks.'
              : 'You\u2019re offline — and this page is still fully here. That\u2019s the whole point.';
          };
          window.addEventListener('online', update);
          window.addEventListener('offline', update);
          update();
        };
        if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
          document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', initOfflineProof);
        } else {
          initOfflineProof();
        }
      </script>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 1120px;">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal="up">What's inside</p>
      <h2 data-reveal="up">The same planner you'd own</h2>
      <p data-reveal="up" style="max-width: 68ch; line-height: 1.7;">
        Open the demo and try it the way you'd use it: check in your energy for
        the day, pick three priorities, break a big task into micro-steps, log
        a habit streak, sketch a budget entry. Everything you see below is a
        screenshot of the running product with its sample data.
      </p>

      <div class="shots" data-reveal="up">
        <ScreenshotFigure
          src="/screenshots/planner-dashboard.svg"
          alt="Screenshot of the planner's Today view: a welcome greeting, stat cards for tasks completed, focus time, habit streak and energy check-in, plus today's top three priorities and an energy check-in panel, with sample data loaded."
          caption="The Today view: priorities, stats and energy check-in at a glance."
        />
        <ScreenshotFigure
          src="/screenshots/planner-tasks.svg"
          alt="Screenshot of the planner's Tasks and Micro-Steps view showing sample tasks with high, medium and low priority labels and an All, Open, Completed filter."
          caption="Tasks & Micro-Steps: priorities and filters, powered by sample entries."
        />
      </div>
      <p class="small muted">
        These screenshots were captured just before the Plenivostudio rename and
        still show the previous "Digitali" branding — the product itself is the
        same planner you can open in the live demo above.
      </p>

      <div class="card demo-limits" data-reveal="up">
        <h2>Demo limitations, stated plainly</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Sample data, not your life.</strong> The demo comes
            pre-loaded with example entries so you can explore. A purchased copy
            starts fresh — yours from the first click.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Separate storage.</strong> Demo changes live in their own
            storage area in your browser. They cannot leak into a purchased
            copy, and you can wipe them any time from Settings.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Loads once, then runs offline.</strong> The demo needs one
            page load to reach your browser; after that it works with no
            internet connection, just like the purchased file.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/downloads/demo.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Open the live demo
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink, #16181d);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .small {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .muted {
    color: #55565e;
  }
  .demo-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
  }
  /* Local notice styles so the page renders correctly regardless of the
     global stylesheet build. */
  .notice {
    border: 1.5px solid var(--line, #e5e3dc);
    border-left: 5px solid var(--indigo, #6554d9);
    background: #f4f2fd;
    border-radius: var(--radius, 12px);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  /* Local definition of the demo frame so the page renders correctly
     regardless of the global stylesheet build. */
  .demo-frame {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: max(420px, min(78vh, 860px));
    border: 1px solid var(--line, #e5e3dc);
    border-radius: var(--radius, 12px);
    background: #fff;
  }
  .shots {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .shots :global(figure) {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .shots :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--line, #e5e3dc);
    border-radius: var(--radius, 12px);
    background: #fff;
  }
  .shots :global(figcaption) {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: #55565e;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .demo-limits {
    padding: 2rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .demo-limits h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .demo-limits ul {
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }
  .demo-limits li + li {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }
  /* Offline proof widget: warm paper card, flat colors, no gradients. */
  .offline-proof {
    padding: 2rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .offline-proof .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .offline-proof h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .offline-proof p {
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .offline-status {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink, #16181d);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line, #e5e3dc);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line, #e5e3dc);
    padding: 1rem 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .offline-dot {
    flex: none;
    width: 0.85rem;
    height: 0.85rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #2e7d4f;
    transition: background-color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .offline-dot.is-offline {
    background: var(--indigo, #6554d9);
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .offline-dot {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .offline-proof {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
    .demo-limits {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
